{"cwd": "/sandbox/runs/harbor-dispatch/runs/eval-INC-94-r1-instincts/harbor-dispatch", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"content": [{"text": "Excellent! INC-94 has been fixed. Here's what I did:\n\n**Problem:** The overlap detection in `BerthSchedule.book()` was using `<=` comparisons, which incorrectly rejected back-to-back bookings (where one ends exactly when another starts).\n\n**Solution:** Changed the `overlaps()` function to use strict `<` comparisons instead:\n- Before: `a.start.getTime() <= b.end.getTime() && b.start.getTime() <= a.end.getTime()`\n- After: `a.start.getTime() < b.end.getTime() && b.start.getTime() < a.end.getTime()`\n\nThis allows bookings that touch at their endpoints (e.g., one ending at noon and another starting at noon) while still preventing genuine overlaps.\n\n**Testing:** Added a test case to verify back-to-back bookings work, and all 27 tests pass.", "type": "text"}], "id": "msg_011CfV9KjuqpHJVC3vEgct1v", "model": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "role": "assistant"}, "sessionId": "49fd7b86-4e8f-47e5-af24-554cbe370d71", "timestamp": "2026-09-28T03:41:22.016Z", "type": "assistant"}
